A||||5||CUTTER||3.1 upgrade from 2.8, need info||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||05-26-2000||01:50 AM||||Im thinking of making my 2.8 a 3.1 what would I need to do this, how much would it cost and where can I get the kit? also, what would be the specs on the 3.1 upgrade compared to the 2.8?<BR>Thanks, Shane||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||05-26-2000||09:06 AM||||You're in luck, several members have done this and will have plenty of info for you. I think the Fiero Store and maybe FOCOA might sell a kit, but you don't have to use a kit. The main things needed is a 3.1 crank, pistons, and flywheel. Cost is not much more than a normal rebuild. Unless you spend a lot of money on head work and other hotrod items, my guess is that the increase in displacement might give you up to about a 20 hp/tq gain.||||reg||1
Z||000002||80's BOY||05-26-2000||10:17 AM||||my suggestion: it's not worth it. if i could do it all over again i would go v8 archie style. or at least northstar. i remember thinking how much those kits were, and now over$2500 later i'm still considering it. if you are a hp freak, go big. if you love the 60 degree block, stroke it. it comes down to that. i'm just a little dissapointed that after all that cash and hours and hours of shop time i gave to it, i still can't beat a stupid mustang at the light.||||reg||13
Z||000003||N_Man||05-26-2000||11:16 PM||||I am right in the middle of mine.  <BR>Its no more work then rebuilding the 2.8<P>I took mine to a machine shop that provides a parts package and asked for the 3.1 crank and silvolite pistons to match .<P>Same price, Same amount of work, hopefully more power.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Eric||05-26-2000||11:41 PM||||The kind of power you get from a mildly built V6 cannot compare to a V8.  You shouldn't expect mind blowing results.  At best you'll feel a little extra push, not a "I gotta learn to drive all over again cause this thing has sooo much power."  If you just are expecting a little more than what a basic rebuild can provide with little extra cost, than the 3.1 is right for you.<P>Part numbers on my 3.1 can be found by searching for "This is what's in my 3.2" or "This is what's in my 3.1" (I can't remember what I named the thread).<P>One thing you will do is drive harder.  If you use good components in your motor this shouldn't be a problem.  That extra push is about +40 or so lb/ft of torque and it is, believe it or not, enough to notice in the good ole A$$-O-METER.||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||05-27-2000||10:30 AM||||Cutter, you may want to checkout ebay. I haven't been there in a while, but everyonce in a while a 3.2 Master rebuild kit pops up. The person is from Texas, if I remember right he goes by "benchshooter." He claims to have lots of experience rebuilding 2.8's inot 3.2's, so you may want to do a search. I just woke up, so I may be wrong, but the starting bid was always $750.<BR>Good luck!!!||||reg||7
